   r² = 1.655 × 10^11 m²
   r = sqrt(1.655 × 10^11) ≈ 12,865 meters

2. **Calculate the mass of the satellite (m):**
   Using the gravitational force formula:
   F = m * g * (r/R)
   3600 N = m * 9 m/s² * (12,865 m / 6,371,000 m)
   3600 = m * 9 * 0.00202
   3600 = m * 0.01818
   m = 3600 / 0.01818 ≈ 197,660 kg

