The most precise method for measuring the strong coupling constant (αs) in particle physics experiments is through a combination of techniques, particularly the precision measurements of the anomalous magnetic moment of the muon (LEptospin) and the measurements of the gluon jet cross-section in the measurements at the Large Hadron Collider ( Heavy-flavor production). These methods are used in comparison with the Standard Model predictions, which involve the value of αs.",ground_truth_similarity,"# Task Description
